    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-1,\\ b=0,\\ c=4$.",
      "worked": "The curve passes through $(1,3)$ and $(2,0)$, and the tangent at $(2,0)$ has gradient $-4$. Since $y'=2ax+b$,\n$$\\begin{align*}a+b+c&=3\\\\4a+2b+c&=0\\\\4a+b&=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtracting the first equation from the second gives $3a+b=-3$. Hence\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=-1\\\\b&=0\\\\c&=4.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
